  "summary": "The desktop app with six machines paired, one in each state a machine's connection reads in, and something new at a machine and in a section at once: what the Machine state and “New” marks variants are compared on. The NUC answers directly (Connected); the workstation only through the room (Through the room); the Mac mini proves itself only after 3 s, so it is still being checked that long on each load (Checking…; the web gives up on a machine after 4 s, so one checked for good can't be had; the card makes it answer at once); the old laptop is off (Not connected); the Raspberry Pi no longer has this device among its own (Not paired, once the page asks it and is refused); and the laboratory's server, with a long name, was paired without encryption at its local network's address (Connected, and Not encrypted). This computer's local host runs, in use; the card walks it through Running, Starting…, Not working, Not running and Not prepared. Seeded too: the models in use and three not used for 12, 45 and 120 days, and ElevenLabs' key connected, OpenAI's not. New, and nothing else: Codex just found on the NUC (a mark on the gear, on Settings' machines, on the NUC and on the agent itself), and a setting from What's new, the speech language (set up on the release before; it shows once a transcription model is ready, which the seeded ones are). Every other machine's agents, and this computer's, are connected or not, none just found.",
